      en: 'FIFA announced 15 new World Cup rules for 2026 edition: (1) 48 teams split into 12 groups of 4 (NOT 16 groups of 3, abandoned in March 2025), (2) top 2 per group + 8 best 3rd = 32-team knockout, (3) 5 substitutions + 1 concussion sub, (4) stoppage time calculation updated (avg +5.2 min/match in 2022 → 2026 target 7+ min), (5) R32 matchup matrix predetermined, (6) VAR offside semi-automated 2.0, (7) captaincy armband 8 types allowed, (8) water/bev breaks temp > 32°C, (9) goal-line technology 1.5mm precision upgrade, (10) handball interpretation tightened, plus 5 more. Full illustrated examples + impact prediction.',
